  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「モンパノキ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A2%E3%83%B3%E3%83%91%E3%83%8E%E3%82%AD",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107362405,
      "text": "モンパノキ は、ムラサキ科キダチルリソウ属の常緑低木〜小高木。別名、ハマムラサキノキ（浜紫の木）。シノニムの argentea は「銀色の」の意味で、葉や若い枝に銀色の毛があることに由来する。中国名は、銀毛樹。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Heliotropium arboreum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliotropium_arboreum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1367421106,
      "text": "Heliotropium arboreum is a species of flowering plant in the family Heliotropiaceae. It is native to tropical Asia including southern China, Madagascar, northern Australia, and most of the atolls and high islands of Micronesia and Polynesia. Common names include velvetleaf soldierbush, tree heliotrope, veloutier, and octopus bush. It is a shrub or small tree typical of littoral zones reaching a height of 3.6 m (12 ft), with a spread of about 5 m (16 ft)."
    }
  },
